details.image_prompt:
[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two matte ceramic plates set on an aged oak table with visible grain and slight wear. The camera angle is 3/4 overhead, capturing the full volume of the food. In the foreground, a portion of fluffy cooked quinoa forms a base on the plate, sitting side-by-side with several browned beef and lentil meatballs, not stacked, allowing each component to be clearly identifiable. The meatballs are coated in a rustic, vibrant red crushed tomato sauce that pools naturally around the edges. Diced zucchini, sautéed to a tender, slightly softened state, is interspersed among the meatballs. The dish is garnished with a fresh, organic scattering of chopped parsley. The background plate is slightly out of focus, mirroring the first. A worn wooden spoon rests casually on the table near a small, crumpled linen napkin. Soft, natural side light from a window to the left creates gentle shadows and highlights the glistening, natural sheen of the olive oil-infused tomato sauce. The scene includes slight, realistic imperfections like a small sauce drip on the rim and a few stray parsley leaves on the wood surface. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, and authentic. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a high-end printed cookbook."
  }
]
